    "text": "<p>Number of electrophillic centres in the given compound is___</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0210_b07575b57485.png\" style=\"width: 215px; height: 130px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp;Electrophilic centre are areas of low electron density. Most often they are atoms which contain a full of partial positive charge. In the given structure the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>CN</mi></math> group, the Keto group &amp; the double bond in conjugation with Keto group are the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> electrophilic centres.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0210_456d57173642.png\" style=\"width: 217px; height: 186px;\" /></p>"
  }
